[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known with one fix queued. Read by tenant, form and what the reporters actually wrote,
it holds three problems. Each now has its own ticket:

| problem | ticket | reports | state |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Parser reads day-first dates month first | [megarepo#1](https://github.com/mslusarkiewicz/megarepo/issues/1) | 374 | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| booking-v3 form hint says `MM/DD/YYYY`, form reads day first | [megarepo#2](https://github.com/mslusarkiewicz/megarepo/issues/2) | 33 | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |
| Dates shift by a day: timezone handling | [megarepo#3](https://github.com/mslusarkiewicz/megarepo/issues/3) | 5 | **open**: no fix |

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October with parser fixed and hint won't fix. The timezone reports were never
part of either decision, and the parser fix does not touch them. megarepo#3 stays open.
</Callout>

## What the table below counts

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

`CauseTable` places a report by its tenant and channel, so it has only two causes. Its
**parser 379 = 374 parser + 5 timezone**: the five reports in the desk's `oneDayMove` notes
(R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) come from day-first tenants through app or email,
so the table files them under `parser`, and its footnote counts them. Their text shows no day/month
swap: a date moved by one day, or the same meeting landed on different days in Lisbon and Toronto.

R-41236 is in that group as a **time problem, not a literal one-day shift**: "the invite arrived before
I made the booking". No date in it moved by a day; the clock was wrong, which is the same timezone
handling.

Its **hint 33** is megarepo#2 as it stands.

## Lessons

- A subject line says how a report felt, not what caused it. Place reports by tenant, form and text.
- Intake's tag is a guess: 23 parser reports came in tagged `hint`.

